>   OPTIONS=name:Klepto
>
>To get a human female rogue named Klepto.  You can then put other groups of 
>options lines in the file, and "comment out" all but one group by putting a 
>"#" in front of each line.  You can then switch between different saved games 
>by putting a comment in front of your current name, and uncommenting another 
>name line.

Same thing works in Window$ in the "nethack.rc" file. You can also put
multiple attributes on a single line to make it simpler (this works
also in *nix). The relevant part of my file looks like this:

OPTIONS=gender:male
#OPTIONS=name:Dutch,role:Archeologist
#OPTIONS=name:Fezzik,role:Barbarian
OPTIONS=name:Garg,role:Caveman
#OPTIONS=name:Aragorn,role:Ranger
#OPTIONS=name:Fagan,role:Rogue
#OPTIONS=name:Mitsubishi,role:Samurai,align:lawful

So, I'm always playing a male character; once I take out the comment
mark, I have my name and role set. With Samurai, I also have alignment
set (can't recall; this may be redundant--can Samurai be other than
lawful?). I could also add "race:<foo>" on the same line if I wanted
to specify race. Separate various settings by commas.

